{"name":"Shanghai Silk","hex":"#c8dfc3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shanghai","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To force or trick someone to go somewhere or do something against their will or interest, particularly:\n\nTo press-gang sailors, especially  for shipping or fishing work.\n\n To trick a suspect into entering a jurisdiction in which they can be lawfully arrested.\n To transfer a serviceman against their will.","To press-gang sailors, especially  for shipping or fishing work."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breed of chicken with large bodies, long legs, and feathered shanks.","A kind of daub."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shanghai"},{"term":"silk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fine fiber excreted by the silkworm or other arthropod (such as a spider).","A thread or yarn made from silk fibers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To develop silk.","To remove the silk from (corn)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shanghai","blocks":[{"text":"Shanghai is a provincial-level direct-administered municipality in China. It has a population of 30,050,000 in the urban area as of 2026, thus making it China's most populous city and more broadly the fifth-largest city in the world by population. The city is located on the southern estuary of the Yangtze River, with the Huangpu River bisecting the city."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Huangpu_Park_20124-Shanghai_%2832208802494%29.jpg/330px-Huangpu_Park_20124-Shanghai_%2832208802494%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai","wikidata":"Q8686"},{"title":"Silk","blocks":[{"text":"Silk is a natural protein fiber, some forms of which can be woven or knitted into textiles. The protein fiber of silk is composed mainly of fibroin (75-80%) and a smaller coating of sericin (20-25%). It is most commonly produced from the cocoons of certain insect larvae. The best-known silk is obtained from the cocoons of the larvae of the mulberry silkworm Bombyx mori, which are reared in captivity (sericulture)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Silk_raw_01a.jpg/330px-Silk_raw_01a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk","wikidata":"Q37681"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg/500px-Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg/1280px-Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg/500px-Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg/500px-2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg/1280px-2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg/500px-2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_mornin